      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- degree-granting department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- graduate-level subjects: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL\n- range of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- variance of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- range of total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- variance of total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- standard deviation of total units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- Biology: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- Chemistry: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"biology and chemistry department\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry', 'Biology')\"\n- \"Biology\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '7'\"\n- \"Course 7\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Biology'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the range and variance of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department? Please provide the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students.\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND scd.COURSE_LEVEL = 'G' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrolled_range DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, provide the department name and the range, variance, and standard deviation of the total units for subjects offered by that department, considering only subjects with more than 0 total units, where the department is degree granting, and excluding the Biology and Chemistry departments.\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance, STDDEV(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_stddev FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sos.OFFER_DEPT_CODE WHERE sos.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sos.OFFER_DEPT_NAME NOT IN ('Biology', 'Chemistry') GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each degree-granting department (excluding Biology and Chemistry), what is the range and variance of the number of enrolled students in the graduate-level subjects offered by that department, as well as the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects with more than 0 total units? Please provide the department name, the range of enrolled students, the variance of enrolled students, the range of total units, the variance of total units, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
