      "content": "The database connection is persistently unavailable (authentication error on every attempt), so live verification is not possible. However, the semantic-network evidence is conclusive: metric **dw_1165** contains the exact precedent SQL for the enrolled-students part (TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, `COURSE_LEVEL='G'`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7'`), and the hint decomposition provides the exact precedent for the total-units part (SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, `TOTAL_UNITS > 0`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME NOT IN ('Biology','Chemistry')`). I'll combine both at department-name granularity with an inner join (which also enforces the Biology+Chemistry exclusion overall).\n\n---\n\n# Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables**\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: Textbook Information Program subject offerings — one row per subject per term in textbook-program scope. Key columns: `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject; used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\").\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: Department dimension — one row per academic department. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N' flag).\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION**: Catalog course descriptions. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `COURSE_LEVEL` ('U' undergraduate / 'G' graduate), `GRADUATE_LEVEL`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (course-level flag — distinct from the department-level flag).\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE**: Subject-code lookup (`SUBJECT_CODE`, `COURSE_NUMBER`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`). Listed in gold tables but not required by either subquery decomposition.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY**: Subject-level rollup per term. Key columns: `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject\"), `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`.\n\n**Metrics (precedents)**\n- **dw_1165**: contains verbatim the enrolled-students dispersion subquery (range/variance of TIP `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` per degree-granting department, graduate-level courses, excluding Biology code '7').\n- **dw_1212**: STDDEV of `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS` with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0` per department — confirms the units-dispersion pattern on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.\n- **dw_1393**: VARIANCE + STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS per department/year — same dispersion idiom.\n- **dw_2151**: per-department AVG/VARIANCE of total units for degree-granting departments excluding Biology ('7').\n\n**Concepts / Column Concepts**\n- **concept_subject_offering_facts**: groups TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, catalog tables — same subject identity, different granularity/enrollment semantics.\n- **concept_department_dimension**: SIS_DEPARTMENT vs STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (SIS_DEPARTMENT carries `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`).\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures**: `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (headcount) vs `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (registrar). The question's \"enrolled students\" maps to `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` per the hint mapping.\n- **column_concept_total_units**: TOTAL_UNITS replicated across catalog/registrar tables; hint maps \"total units\" to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\n- **column_concept_department_name**: DEPARTMENT_NAME (lookup) vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME (offering tables) — same academic value domain.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\nGraph traversal confirmed: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins SIS_DEPARTMENT (via OFFER_DEPT_CODE) and belongs to concept_subject_offering_facts and concept_course_material_programs; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY joins SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, and carries column_concept_total_units. SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE is a documented join.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Enrollment measure candidates**: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (textbook-program scope, subject/term grain) vs SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS / SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (registrar scope). The hint mapping explicitly anchors \"enrolled students\" → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, and dw_1165's precedent uses exactly that.\n\n**3b. Fitness**: The task requires (i) range/variance of enrolled students for graduate-level subjects of degree-granting departments excluding Biology → SUPPORTED only by the TIP+COURSE_LEVEL='G' join (dw_1165 precedent); (ii) range/variance/stddev of TOTAL_UNITS > 0 excluding Biology+Chemistry → SUPPORTED by SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (dw_1212 precedent); TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED has no units columns → NOT-SUPPORTED for (ii).\n\n**3c. Wording anchoring**: \"degree-granting department\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' (domain knowledge); \"graduate-level\" → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL='G'; \"Biology\" → DEPARTMENT_CODE '7' / name 'Biology'; \"Chemistry\" → name 'Chemistry'. The SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION join fans out rows per department (many courses), but MAX/MIN/VARIANCE are invariant to row duplication — the dw_1165 precedent accepts this.\n\n**3d. Precedent usage**: enrolled-range/variance on TIP: 1 precedent (dw_1165, verbatim). TOTAL_UNITS dispersion on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: dw_1212 (AVG/STDDEV with TOTAL_UNITS>0).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nSIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical degree-granting filter dimension; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves textbook-program enrollment questions; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY serves unit-structure statistics; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION supplies course-level ('G') filtering.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase-1 entities investigated: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (semantic_get + graph); dw_1165, dw_2151, dw_1212, dw_1393 (semantic_get); concepts/column-concepts (semantic_get/search results). mysql_query attempted 7 times — all failed with DB authentication error (noted explicitly).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a/6b**: Combine the two gold subqueries as CTEs, inner-join on DEPARTMENT_NAME. Subquery 1 (TIP-based enrolled dispersion, excludes Biology via code '7'); Subquery 2 (SUMMARY-based units dispersion, excludes Biology+Chemistry via OFFER_DEPT_NAME). The inner join enforces the overall \"excluding Biology and Chemistry\". SELECT exactly: department name, enrolled range, enrolled variance, units range, units variance, units stddev. Use bare STDDEV() and VARIANCE() per hints.\n\n**6c**: Data — column existence verified via retrieved column definitions; fan-out from SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION is harmless for MAX/MIN/VARIANCE. Semantic-network — join keys documented in graph edges; dw_1165 is a verbatim precedent. Business — matches the two documented subquery decompositions.\n\n**6d**: No tie-breakers needed; precedents are unambiguous. Caveat: live DB verification was impossible due to persistent authentication failure.\n\n",
